@page "/programming-concepts/http-logger"


<div class="div-app">
    <p>Storing logs is a fundamental part of any application. It allows us to look back in time and pin-point specific issues that have come up.</p>
    <p>.NET Core offers a simple way to configure this. For the purpose of this demonstration, you must set the configuration of "logging" to true (if set to false), and re-start the app.</p>
    <p>The reason why it is not set to true is to avoid including a configuration that will only reduce the functionality of the app and it is only pertinent in certain articles of this application.</p>
    <p>The article used to research the functionality is the following: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/http-logging/?view=aspnetcore-8.0">Microsoft Documentation</a></p>
</div>


